# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF on every platform. Prettier is configured
# with `endOfLine: "lf"` (.prettierrc), so without this a Windows checkout under the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` hands Prettier CRLF copies of files git stores as LF, and `format:check`
# reports the entire repository as unformatted -- 786 files on the first run of
# `.github/workflows/compatibility.yml`, none of which any commit had touched. `text=auto` still
# lets git detect binaries, so the PNG baselines under `tests/visual/__screenshots__` and
# `media/` are left byte-for-byte alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Committed webview payload fixtures are byte-compared, not parsed-and-compared:
# `webviewFixtureGate.ts` re-records each one and asserts the regenerated STRING equals the
# committed file. `serializeWebviewFixture` always emits LF, so on a checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) the working-tree copy comes back CRLF and every
# fixture reports drift the moment anyone runs the gate -- a false failure that no code change
# caused and no regeneration can fix. Pinning `eol=lf` keeps the checked-out bytes the recorded
# bytes on every platform. Redundant with the repository-wide rule above and deliberately kept:
# these files need LF for correctness, not just for tidiness, so narrowing the rule above must
# not silently narrow this one.
tests/visual/fixtures/**/*.json text eol=lf
